d guards. The iff has no minimizer premise. The converse uses |G(s)|<=1-s, weighted Fubini and convexity of the control-value functional. Arbitrary curves with contact properties need not arise from this gamma; the criterion alone neither proves full support nor constructs a minimizer.","citation_ids":["support_optimality_chl","support_optimality_chen","support_variation_source","support_model_source"],"evidence_ids":["support_optimality_warrant_20261024"],"id":"support.optimality_criterion","kind":"claim","label":"An exact first-order criterion for the same admissible coefficient","locator":"CHL arXiv:1609.04368v4 Proposition 4, printed p.14; long reasoning record §3.5","source_id":"chl2018_zero_temperature","statement":"For an admissible gamma in the pure zero-field SK normalization, let Phi, X and q(t)=E[Phi_x(t,X_t)^2] be the control value, diffusion and moment for this same gamma. Let mu([0,t])=gamma(t), S=supp_[0,1)(mu), and G(s)=integral_s^1(q(t)-t)dt. Then gamma minimizes the zero-temperature Parisi functional if and only if G(s)>=0 for every s<1 and G=0 on S.","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/nodes/support.optimality_criterion","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/nodes/support.optimality_criterion","id":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/edges/%5B%22support.optimality_criterion%22%2C%22support.first_variation%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","kind":"supports","record_ref":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/edges/%5B%22support.optimality_criterion%22%2C%22support.first_variation%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","semantic_class":"curated_argument_support","to":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/nodes/support.first_variation"},{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a27943